    back: "In cytoplasm: Glucose (6-C) breaks down into Pyruvate (3-C) + Energy.\n1. Absence of Oxygen (Yeast fermentation): Pyruvate → Ethanol + CO₂ + Energy (2 ATP).\n2. Lack of Oxygen (Human muscle cells during vigorous exercise): Pyruvate → Lactic acid + Energy. Accumulation of lactic acid causes muscle cramps.\n3. Presence of Oxygen (Mitochondria - Aerobic): Pyruvate → CO₂ + H₂O + Energy (36-38 ATP).",
