    front: "Explain Double Circulation in the human heart and why it is necessary for birds and mammals.",
    back: "Double circulation means blood passes through the heart twice during each complete cardiac cycle:\n1. Pulmonary Circulation: Deoxygenated blood from Right Ventricle → Lungs (via Pulmonary Artery) → Oxygenated blood to Left Atrium (via Pulmonary Veins).\n2. Systemic Circulation: Oxygenated blood from Left Ventricle → Body organs (via Aorta) → Deoxygenated blood to Right Atrium (via Vena Cava).\nWhy necessary: Completely separates oxygenated and deoxygenated blood, ensuring high energy supply to maintain constant body temperature (warm-blooded animals).",
