    back: "A nephron is the basic structural and functional filtration unit of the human kidney.\nThree steps in urine formation:\n1. Ultrafiltration: Glomerulus filters blood under pressure into Bowman's capsule (forming initial filtrate containing glucose, amino acids, salts, and water).\n2. Selective Reabsorption: Useful substances (glucose, amino acids, major water) are reabsorbed into surrounding peritubular capillaries along the tubular part.\n3. Tubular Secretion: Extra ions (K⁺, H⁺, drugs) are secreted into the collecting tubule to form concentrated urine.",
