    subjectLabel: "Science",
    topic: "Our Environment",
    front: "State Lindeman's 10% Law of energy transfer in an ecosystem and why food chains are limited to 3-4 trophic levels.",
    back: "10% Law: Only 10% of the energy entering a trophic level is stored and available for transfer to the next higher trophic level. The remaining 90% is lost as heat to the environment during respiration, digestion, movement, and life maintenance.\nLimitation: Because 90% is lost at each step, after 3 or 4 trophic levels, the amount of remaining usable energy is too small to support another viable trophic population.",
    keywords: ["Only 10% transferred", "90% lost as metabolic heat", "Little energy remains after 3-4 steps"],
    chapterLink: "/resources/our-environment/"
  },
