    front: "What is Ozone (O₃), how is it formed in the stratosphere, and how do CFCs deplete it?",
    back: "Ozone is a triatomic molecule of oxygen that shields Earth from harmful ultraviolet (UV) radiation.\nFormation:\n1. High-energy UV radiation splits molecular oxygen: O₂ --UV--> O + O.\n2. Free oxygen atom combines with O₂: O + O₂ → O₃ (Ozone).\nDepletion: Chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs) release active chlorine radicals upon UV exposure in the stratosphere. One chlorine radical catalytically breaks down thousands of ozone molecules into ordinary oxygen.",
    keywords: ["UV splits O₂ into O + O", "O + O₂ → O₃", "CFCs release active chlorine radicals"],
    chapterLink: "/resources/our-environment/"
