    back: "• Simile: Explicit comparison between two unlike things using 'like' or 'as' (e.g., 'as proud as a peacock', 'face ashen like that of a corpse').\n• Metaphor: Direct implicit comparison without using 'like' or 'as' (e.g., 'The fog comes on little cat feet', 'pad of velvet quiet').\n• Personification: Giving human characteristics/feelings to non-human objects or abstractions (e.g., 'He stalks in his vivid stripes... ignoring visitors' in A Tiger in the Zoo).",
